{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792349939,"nonce":"a3zdb7xAgBnfmhwWgobVAqr/190=","title":"Explorer context menus, for files and folders, with a place for extensions to add items","message":"Reported by the user, 2026-10-18: file items and folders in the Explorer have no context menus.\n\nBuilt in\n- File: Open, Open in a new tab beside, Copy path, Copy relative path, Reveal in the file manager, Rename…, Delete…\n- Folder: New file…, New folder…, Rename…, Delete…, Copy path, Copy relative path, Reveal, Collapse all, Refresh.\n- The project root: New file…, New folder…, Refresh.\n- A name is asked for in a small prompt over the tree (Enter accepts, Escape cancels, a clash or a bad character is said in the prompt). Delete asks first and says what goes, and an open tab of a deleted or renamed file follows it or closes.\n- Opens on right click, and on the menu key or Shift+F10 with the row selected; closes on Escape, a click away, or a choice. Destructive items in the error colour; separators between groups; keys shown beside items that have one.\n\nContribution point\n- `explorer/context` is where an extension's menu items are added (see the issue on extension hooks and contributions). An item has a title, a command, and a `when`: the kind (file or folder), the file's extension, a name pattern. Contributed items go in a group of their own below the built-in ones.\n\nDone when: each item works on a project in a scripted run (snapshots show the menu for a file and for a folder in both themes, and after Rename and New file the tree and the tabs are right), and a contributed item appears for the files it names and for no others.","files":null}]}